<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <item>
      type        : CONFIG_CHECK
      description : "Check for multicast-routing or pim"
      item        : "ip (multicast-routing|pim)"
    </item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <item>
      type        : CONFIG_CHECK
      description : "1.93 CISC-RT-000910"
      info        : "The Cisco Multicast Source Discovery Protocol (MSDP) router must be configured to authenticate all received MSDP packets.

GROUP ID: V-216729
RULE ID: SV-216729r855835

MSDP peering with customer network routers presents additional risks to the core, whether from a rogue or misconfigured MSDP-enabled router. MSDP password authentication is used to validate each segment sent on the TCP connection between MSDP peers, protecting the MSDP session against the threat of spoofed packets being injected into the TCP connection stream."
      solution    : "Configure the router to authenticate MSDP messages as shown in the following example:

R2(config)#ip msdp password peer x.1.28.8 xxxxxxxxxxxx"
      reference   : "800-171r3|03.05.02,800-53|IA-3,800-53r5|IA-3,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001958,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ITSG-33|IA-3,ITSG-33|IA-3a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.4.3,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-216729r855835_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000910,TBA-FIISB|27.1,Vuln-ID|V-216729"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26261"
      item        : "ip msdp password peer [^ ]+ [^ ]+"
    </item>
  </then>

  <else>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "1.93 CISC-RT-000910"
      info        : "The Cisco Multicast Source Discovery Protocol (MSDP) router must be configured to authenticate all received MSDP packets.

GROUP ID: V-216729
RULE ID: SV-216729r855835

MSDP peering with customer network routers presents additional risks to the core, whether from a rogue or misconfigured MSDP-enabled router. MSDP password authentication is used to validate each segment sent on the TCP connection between MSDP peers, protecting the MSDP session against the threat of spoofed packets being injected into the TCP connection stream."
      solution    : "Configure the router to authenticate MSDP messages as shown in the following example:

R2(config)#ip msdp password peer x.1.28.8 xxxxxxxxxxxx"
      reference   : "800-171r3|03.05.02,800-53|IA-3,800-53r5|IA-3,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001958,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ITSG-33|IA-3,ITSG-33|IA-3a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.4.3,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-216729r855835_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000910,TBA-FIISB|27.1,Vuln-ID|V-216729"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26261"
    </report>
  </else>
</if>

